App::karr::Git DESCRIPTION (the paragraph on the CLI transport fallback)
says:

    because libgit2/libssh2 doesn't read ~/.ssh/config and can't run a
    ProxyCommand -- directives like Host aliases, IdentityFile, and
    insteadOf only take effect through the CLI.

The list mixes two different config files, and the git-config half of it
is wrong: url.<base>.insteadOf is applied by libgit2 itself. Measured on
libgit2 1.9.3 (the floor #174 pinned), with KARR_NO_CLI_FALLBACK=1 so
that no git CLI could be involved:

    git config url."$work/".insteadOf karrboard:
    git remote add alias karrboard:board.git
    remote_has_board("alias")  ->  1        # native, rewrite applied

Without a matching insteadOf rule, the same shape goes to DNS for the
literal host ("failed to resolve address for karrboard"), so the 1 above
can only come from libgit2 having done the rewrite. A rewrite pointing at
a path that does not exist fails as "unsupported URL protocol", which is
what made the first reading of this look the other way round.

What is genuinely CLI-only is the ~/.ssh/config half: Host aliases and
the IdentityFile, User and Port under them, plus ProxyCommand. libssh2
takes board:karr.git for the literal host "board".

Found while doing #203, which rewrote the same argument for
remote_has_board (there it is now stated as the ssh-config half only,
with a note that insteadOf is not part of it). This ticket is the
DESCRIPTION paragraph that still governs fetch/push, left alone because
#203 was scoped to the probe and to the four ssh-timeout doc sites.

Worth checking at the same time: pushInsteadOf, and whether libgit2
applies insteadOf to ssh:// and https:// URLs as well as to the local
paths measured here.
DESCRIPTION paragraph rewritten in lib/App/karr/Git.pm; Changes entry under {{$NEXT}}. Both open questions answered by measurement on libgit2 1.9.3 (raw Git::Native, git_remote_lookup + git_remote_push, no CLI anywhere in the loop), throwaway repos under the scratchpad only.

Q1 pushInsteadOf: YES, libgit2 applies it. Two bare repos A and B behind a
`git daemon --enable=receive-pack`; url.git://.../A/.insteadOf=karrsplit: and
url.git://.../B/.pushInsteadOf=karrsplit:, remote karrsplit:board.git. Fetch
reached A, push landed in B. An explicit remote.<name>.pushurl behaves the
same way over git://.

Q2 ssh:// and https:// : YES, both, and on both sides of a rule. As the URL
being rewritten, ssh://karrhost.invalid/board.git and the https:// equivalent
with a matching insteadOf pointing at a valid local bare repo both fetched and
pushed OK, while the identical URLs with the rule removed failed at DNS. As
the rewrite target, karralias:board.git under url.ssh://rewritten.invalid/.insteadOf
(and the https:// twin) failed naming rewritten.invalid, against a control
naming karralias. So it is a textual prefix substitution ahead of any protocol
handling, not a local-path-only feature.

The first pass got Q1 backwards, exactly the way #203 warns about. Measuring
pushInsteadOf with both targets as local paths showed the push landing at the
insteadOf target, which reads as "pushInsteadOf ignored". It is not: libgit2
connects to the push URL (pushInsteadOf aimed at ssh://pushtarget.invalid/
fails naming that host) and its local transport then writes to the fetch URL.
That is behaviour, not prose, so it is #208 rather than a silent fix, and the
new paragraph names it as the one corner that does not hold.

